{"title":"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Halfway through a 100-shot archery tournament, Chelsea leads by 50 points. For each shot a bullseye scores 10 points, with other possible scores being 8, 4, 2, and 0 points. Chelsea always scores at least 4 points on each shot. If Chelsea's next <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> shots are bullseyes she will be guaranteed victory. What is the minimum value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1cdcd819720d948d327ecb767dff769dc1983f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 38 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 40 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 42 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 44 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of points Chelsea currently has. In order to guarantee victory, we must consider the possibility that the opponent scores the maximum amount of points by getting only bullseyes.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/7446b964cde5275bdf791fe97994eb984c2ee262.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}k+ 10n + 4(50-n) &amp;&gt; (k-50) + 50\\cdot{10}\\\\  6n &amp;&gt; 250\\end{align*}\" width=\"317\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe lowest integer value that satisfies the inequality is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/8755b1518d332dd28a36e0fe46caf7d092635c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{42\\ \\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A\">2010 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"